# Cloudflare Workers/Pages static-assets headers.
# .htaccess only applies on Apache/LiteSpeed (Hostinger) — this file is the
# equivalent for the Cloudflare deployment (catering-tools-by-deecstudio).
#
# Strict-Transport-Security forces HTTPS for a full year on every future
# visit, including subdomains — closes the small window where a visitor
# typing the bare domain (no https://) could have their very first request
# go out over plain HTTP before Cloudflare's redirect kicks in. No
# "; preload" — that submits the domain to browsers' hardcoded preload
# list, which is far harder to reverse than this header alone.
#
# script-src allowlists specific inline scripts by their SHA-256 hash
# (the Whop + Meta Pixel base snippets in index.html's <head>) instead of
# using 'unsafe-inline' — every OTHER inline script stays blocked, which
# is what makes this site's XSS surface a non-issue. Edit either snippet
# and its hash goes stale (recompute it and update here + .htaccess, or
# it's silently blocked). main.js's Contact tracking call (fired on every
# WhatsApp CTA click) isn't a third inline script — it's trusted via
# script-src 'self', so it needs no hash. https://t.whop.tw is Whop's
# tracking domain (loads s.js, sends events) — unrelated to the WhatsApp
# CTAs, kept for Whop's own analytics.
# https://connect.facebook.net/https://www.facebook.com are Meta's (loads
# fbevents.js, sends events, serves the <noscript> fallback pixel image).
# facebook.com is also in frame-src/form-action: fbevents.js falls back to
# a hidden iframe/form POST to deliver events when its primary fetch/image
# beacon is blocked (privacy modes, some browsers) — confirmed by testing,
# not guessed. Some other random-looking third-party domains (AWS/GCP
# hostnames) showed up as blocked connect-src attempts during testing —
# NOT allowlisted here on purpose, they don't look like standard Meta
# infrastructure and weren't verified as legitimate.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(self "https://whop.com")
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'sha256-Vj0ZQI6HmRlgG8PCxGgAq25M62GE2IwjbyWbU26rh4Y=' 'sha256-8MexTA4cl23iH+k1us9OYTnOJCky1DyRUzZ+Stho6v4=' https://t.whop.tw https://connect.facebook.net; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://api.fontshare.com https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://api.fontshare.com https://cdn.fontshare.com https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: https://www.facebook.com; frame-src https://whop.com https://www.facebook.com; connect-src 'self' https://whop.com https://t.whop.tw https://www.facebook.com https://connect.facebook.net; frame-ancestors 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self' https://www.facebook.com; object-src 'none'
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains

/*.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate

# stale-while-revalidate/stale-if-error on top of no-cache/must-revalidate:
# if a revalidation request gets cut short (seen on iOS Safari after 2-3
# rapid reloads — it can cancel in-flight requests instead of retrying),
# the browser is explicitly allowed to fall back to the last good cached
# copy instead of ending up with no stylesheet/script at all, which is
# what was producing an unstyled-HTML flash on repeated fast refreshes.
/*.css
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate, stale-while-revalidate=86400, stale-if-error=86400

/*.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate, stale-while-revalidate=86400, stale-if-error=86400

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000
